You remember, la casa?

00:09:30.905 --> 00:09:31.545
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:34.325
The, the, the one with the tips
on how to sound more Italian.

00:09:34.325 --> 00:09:34.595
Yeah.

00:09:35.525 --> 00:09:35.815
Okay.

00:09:35.835 --> 00:09:37.125
Yeah, that's an interesting one.

00:09:37.125 --> 00:09:42.565
So, um, uh, what did I talk about
in the, I talked about la casa.

00:09:42.615 --> 00:09:42.885
Yeah.

00:09:42.885 --> 00:09:44.435
For instance, you mentioned, right.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:44.655
So.

00:09:45.225 --> 00:09:50.944
Like in Spanish, a word like casa has a
very short, stressed first "ah", casa.

00:09:51.655 --> 00:09:55.755
Well, an Italian, and this makes
Italian sound the way it does.

00:09:55.785 --> 00:10:00.645
We tend to make that "ah" make
that stressed vowel longer.

00:10:00.645 --> 00:10:03.165
So it's casa...

00:10:03.405 --> 00:10:03.775
Spanish...

00:10:03.775 --> 00:10:09.575
anytime you would say...

00:10:10.945 --> 00:10:15.255
so you elongate those vowels more and
that's, it makes you sound more italian.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.205
But, but you made the point
that that depending...

00:10:17.265 --> 00:10:17.415
like....

00:10:20.969 --> 00:10:23.859
so depending on the stress in...

00:10:23.949 --> 00:10:27.750
like wherever the stress is,
that, that's where that happens.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.760
So it, it's not automatic that
every time you see casa, it's gonna,

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:31.920
the stress is gonna be the same.

00:10:32.189 --> 00:10:32.610
Yeah, no,

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:33.270
no, exactly.

00:10:33.275 --> 00:10:35.969
So it's usually the last word in
a sentence, but it also depends

00:10:35.974 --> 00:10:38.550
on where the, the emphasis is...

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:41.579
um, but if you say...

00:10:43.425 --> 00:10:44.665
instead of...

00:10:46.075 --> 00:10:52.455
so my friend, so in that case that's
a little bit technical, but yeah,

00:10:52.455 --> 00:10:55.005
it's, uh, uh, that's interesting.

00:10:55.005 --> 00:10:57.225
So, so how does one, how
does one acquire that?

00:10:57.225 --> 00:11:01.215
Does one acquire that by just
doing a lot of listening and

00:11:01.545 --> 00:11:03.055
being attentive to the language?

00:11:03.315 --> 00:11:06.945
Or is it necessary to have
that pointed out or, I guess

00:11:06.945 --> 00:11:08.584
it depends on the individual.

00:11:09.465 --> 00:11:09.765
Yeah.

00:11:09.765 --> 00:11:14.795
I think it depends, and I think it's,
it's a mix of the, of both actually.

00:11:14.895 --> 00:11:19.185
Um, you, of course, you have to do
a lot of listening as we, as you, as

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:23.060
you, you know, teach on your channel.

00:11:23.115 --> 00:11:28.135
But I think it, it, it helps to
have people point things out that

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:29.975
you might not necessarily notice.

00:11:30.735 --> 00:11:32.385
And, uh, yeah, I don't know.

00:11:32.385 --> 00:11:33.065
What do you think?

00:11:33.065 --> 00:11:33.665
Do you think...

00:11:34.845 --> 00:11:39.135
uh, I think, well, you know, I always
quote this, uh, lady who ran the San

00:11:39.135 --> 00:11:42.825
Diego State University Language Department
who said, there's only three things

00:11:42.825 --> 00:11:46.605
that matter in language learning: uh,
the attitude of the learner, the time

00:11:46.605 --> 00:11:50.025
you spend with the language, so not
reading a grammar book in your own

00:11:50.025 --> 00:11:53.835
language, but actually with the language,
reading, speaking, listening, whatever.

00:11:53.895 --> 00:11:55.975
And the third thing is
the ability to notice.

00:11:56.325 --> 00:11:59.550
And I think to some extent the
ability to notice develops if

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:00.930
you put enough time into it.

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:03.540
If you have a, an attitude
that you want to notice, but

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:04.610
some people just don't notice.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.370
The question is, even those people
who don't notice, even if you

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:12.000
point it out, it doesn't mean
they're gonna be able to do it.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.280
So it it's kind of a mixture.

00:12:14.285 --> 00:12:17.490
It's, it's, sometimes it helps,
I, I wouldn't say it doesn't help.

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:20.820
It's like in Russian, the
unaccentuated "o" becomes an "ah",

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:22.620
some people don't notice that.

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:25.740
You point it out, it doesn't
mean they're gonna do it.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:27.890
So I It's a mixture of both.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.920
Um, yeah.

00:12:29.939 --> 00:12:34.560
Another area where I thought we, it was
interesting you showed those circles of...

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:37.350
in other words this whole issue
of how many words do you need?

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:40.260
How do you activate your vocabulary?

00:12:40.319 --> 00:12:43.709
And you had one person on there who was
very much into, you know, every time

00:12:43.709 --> 00:12:47.835
you learn a word, write it out, use
it, which I'm not a big fan of because

00:12:47.835 --> 00:12:49.665
it's, it's gonna limit your vocabulary.

00:12:49.665 --> 00:12:53.385
So there's always this issue of how
much focus on this bits and pieces,

00:12:53.385 --> 00:12:57.045
the details versus how much of the
language are you gonna bring into you.

00:12:57.405 --> 00:12:59.475
Uh, and I think you have
to strike a balance.

00:12:59.805 --> 00:13:03.765
Uh, and you pointed out too that you
have this sort of larger circle of words

00:13:03.765 --> 00:13:06.825
that you know, in a very small number
of words that you're comfortable using.

00:13:07.155 --> 00:13:12.210
Uh, at some point you have to expand
that, and you do that by speaking more,

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:13.410
and you shouldn't be afraid of speaking.

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:17.040
But at the same time, if you have
a very small, larger circle, you'll

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.050
never have much comprehension.

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:22.350
You'll never have, you know, words
that you can eventually use to

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:23.880
increase your active vocabulary.

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:29.190
So there's this constant push and pull
between how much input and how much you

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:30.880
actually have to use what you've learned.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:33.605
Where do you, where do
you see all of this?

00:13:34.255 --> 00:13:39.030
I mean, um, I'm a massive fan of,
uh, I'm, I'm a huge fan of massive

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:44.250
input, uh and I've been, you know,
influenced by, by you on this.

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:47.610
And I think you, you absolutely
need to immerse yourself as much

